'' A BYVAL UDT PARAMETER is a POINTER to a copy the CALLER builds -- but only when the
'' type is non-trivial. Measured: fbc writes 'void T1( struct $2D1* )' for a type with a
'' destructor and 'void T2( struct $2C1 )' for one whose only member is a default
'' constructor, and around the call it emits the copy, the call and the temporary's
'' destructor in that order.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/byval-udt-param.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/byval-udt-param.out
